## 3. Key Takeaways & Defense Recommendations

> [!NOTE]
> **WMI Repository Persistence** is highly effective because standard tools (like Sysinternals Autoruns) may not perform deep registry/repository structure searches for custom namespaces or non-standard class properties.

*   **Detection:** Monitor WMI Repository modifications (`C:\Windows\System32\wbem\Repository\OBJECTS.DATA` file writes) or use PowerShell cmdlets like `Get-CimInstance` to audit custom WMI classes.
*   **Analysis:** When dealing with WMI-stored binaries, always look for Base64 and compression pipelines (`Base64 -> Deflate -> Memory Injection`) commonly used by fileless malware loaders.
